# Forms and onboarding

Form dialogs and onboarding flows use the **rewards plate**, the same leather dialog as DPS Stone event entry. Filter rails and Item Library chrome stay on the parchment recipe in `design.mdc`.

## Reference

- Plate: `.bpb-panel--rewards` in `css/theme.css` (`--bpb-rewards-ink`, `--bpb-rewards-gold`, `--bpb-rewards-gold-bright`, `--bpb-rewards-cream`)
- Worked example: `js/pages/events/enter-wizard.css` and the enter-wizard markup

## Do

- Shell: dark leather plate, gold border, gold corner ticks. Soft dim behind the dialog.
- Title row: Baskerville **bold**, uppercase, tracked, gold. A gold rule with a diamond on each side. Gold × to close.
- Section titles: same gold Baskerville. Not Milonga, and not an OptionsFont cream outline.
- Hints: Baskerville italic, cream.
- Fields: dark well, gold border. A path or file picker uses a **dashed** gold border. The field name is gold; the value is cream.
- Secondary actions: full width, gold outline, cream label, dark fill.
- Stepped flows: a gold rule, the step name in small gold uppercase, then dots. The current step is the filled gold dot.
- An info **i** floats its note. It does not push the section taller.

## Don’t

- Put these dialogs back on parchment Patch3, a green Milonga submit, or a gray/purple form kit
- Use Milonga sticker titles or 26px cream outlines on this plate
- Invent a second plate. Extend `.bpb-panel--rewards` and the enter-wizard type
- Set `scrollbar-color` to the gold/brown pair. Scrollbars stay the items-bag recipe
